## 6. Timing, and when to ramp back up

Hold the reduced level through September and October. Decide on the ramp in the first half of October, and move money in the second half.

That timing follows the calendar. The events that move trading activity are the US Federal Reserve's rate meetings (FOMC), Banco de Mexico's rate decisions and the US midterm elections. September is thin and front-loaded. Late October into mid-November carries the densest run of them in the year.

| Date | Event |
|---|---|
| September 15 to 16 | US Federal Reserve (FOMC), with updated economic projections |
| September 24 | Banco de México rate decision |
| October 27 to 28 | US Federal Reserve (FOMC) |
| **November 3** | **US midterm elections** |
| **November 5** | **Banco de México rate decision** |
| December 8 to 9 | US Federal Reserve (FOMC), with updated economic projections |
| December 17 | Banco de México rate decision |

There is no Federal Reserve meeting in November.

The midterms are the largest scheduled event of the period and their effect is not confined to Mexico. A midterm result reprices expectations for US fiscal policy, trade and rates, which moves the dollar, Treasury yields, equity indices and commodities together. That is the product set these campaigns advertise: the account runs lines for gold, silver and the MT4, MT5 and TradingView platforms, alongside brand and competitor terms. The Banco de México decision two days later adds a Mexico-specific layer in the same week.

The market is already pricing this. VIX futures settled on August 26 with the curve rising through the end of the year.

| Contract | Settlement, August 26, 2026 |
|---|---:|
| August, expiring | 15.61 |
| September | 17.15 |
| October | 18.85 |
| November | 19.60 |
| December | 19.75 |

The October contract matters most for timing. It settles on October 21 and prices expected volatility over the following thirty days, a window that contains the November 3 election. It sits about 21% above the contract expiring now. These are prices rather than forecasts and they move daily, but they establish that the market is not treating the autumn as a continuation of August.

### Lead times set the decision date

| Channel | Time to reach full weight | Start by |
|---|---|---|
| Quantcast and other display advertising | Three to four weeks. The platforms have to rebuild a profile of who to target and then learn which of those people respond | Early to mid October |
| Azerion display | Booking paperwork plus a comparable build-up | Early to mid October |
| Bing search | Days, since intent is captured at the moment of search | Late October |

Search can be raised close to the event, because someone typing a search is already looking. Display cannot. A display audience started on November 1 is still being learned while the November 3 window is happening.

**Recommended sequence.** Hold through September and treat the September 15 to 16 Federal Reserve meeting and the September 24 Banco de Mexico decision as information, without acting on them. Decide the ramp in the first half of October, on one full month of the reduced plan. Rebuild the display channels in the second half of October if the decision is to ramp, so their audiences are working properly before November 3. Increase Bing from late October into November, sized to the demand that actually appears. Reassess in mid-November for December and the new fiscal year.

