## 7. September

The approved September budget is $205,000, an increase of about 64% on August. Three of its lines are not currently running: Meta at $30,000, TikTok at $10,000 and Strategic Partnerships at $40,000.

**We do not recommend the September plan as approved.** Eighty thousand dollars of it, or 39%, is allocated to channels that are not live, two of which have no GGMI performance history to size against.

We recommend running September at the chosen option, $61,000 or $33,500, and holding that level through October. The $80,000 should be deferred rather than cancelled, so it stays available for the October ramp if the evidence supports launching those channels then.

The approved plan in the tracker runs to September, which closes FY26. October onward carries no approved figure, so the October ramp decision and FY27 planning are the same conversation.

